We are looking for a skilled Fullstack Engineer (Frontend focused) for service agreement collaboration (B2B contract) to cooperate with a team dedicated to Network Planning at FlixTrain - building internal tools that help plan the timetable and vehicle allocation, reduce manual processes, and increase productivity. This is a greenfield environment with plenty of room to shape new products from the ground up and explore innovative solutions for our internal users. &nbsp;

Scope of Services &nbsp;

You will independently develop and deliver high-quality frontend features, with occasional backend work, within a self-organized, cross-functional, distributed team. This includes building intuitive user interfaces with a focus on the experience of our internal users. You will also help drive frontend architecture decisions and contribute to technical quality across teams through code reviews and close collaboration. &nbsp;

About the Engagement &nbsp;

• Design and build internal web applications that automate and simplify FlixTrain Network Planning workflows &nbsp;

• Develop modern, responsive user interfaces with React and TypeScript and contribute to a consistent, reusable frontend architecture &nbsp;

• Design and implement backend functionality, including GraphQL APIs, server-side logic and database models &nbsp;

• Work with internal users and stakeholders to understand their needs and turn them into practical product solutions &nbsp;

• Write and maintain automated tests, to ensure reliability and maintainability &nbsp;

• Collaborate with other engineers across a distributed architecture within an Agile environment &nbsp;

• Document technical decisions, solutions and ways of working &nbsp;

About You &nbsp;

Must have: &nbsp;

• Hands-on experience with React (React 19 in our stack) and TypeScript, with a strong command of HTML and CSS &nbsp;

• Experience with an object-oriented backend language. Java is not required, but preferable: Node.js or similar is acceptable, provided you have real backend development experience, not just scripting &nbsp;

• Hands-on experience in backend web application development: building and designing GraphQL APIs, server-side logic and database design &nbsp;

• Experience writing tests and working with test runners such as Vitest &nbsp;

• Understanding of event-driven systems and how to work with them &nbsp;

• Solid written and spoken English skills &nbsp;

• Experience working in an Agile setup &nbsp;

• Curiosity about the business domain. Interest in transportation, logistics or similarly complex domains is a good signal, as is the ability to explain such a domain clearly &nbsp;

Nice to have: &nbsp;

• GraphQL: used in our stack (Spring for GraphQL, Apollo, gql.tada) &nbsp;

• Java and Spring Boot / Spring Framework &nbsp;

• Kafka &nbsp;

• Experience with agentic or AI-assisted coding &nbsp;

Collaboration Model &nbsp;

• Contract type: Cooperation based on a service agreement (B2B/freelance contract), not an employment contract &nbsp;

• Working model: Independent contractor responsible for delivering agreed services and submitting invoices &nbsp;

• Location: Open for contractors based in Poland &nbsp;

